GridCraft VAIO preview 0.8.0

Open GridCraft (VAIO preview) from Office or VAIO App Launcher. Ctrl+O opens
a workbook; Ctrl+S saves. Keep a separate copy when editing important files.
Use the ribbon for formulas, formatting, charts and printing/export to PDF.
The gridcraft-vaio-cli command provides the upstream headless tools.

Measured on the Atom VAIO with a small synthetic budget: GUI cell editing,
formulas/recalculation, bold formatting, a column chart, XLSX save/reopen,
CSV export and PDF export passed. Sorting/filtering, validation, conditional
formatting, frozen panes and a saved PivotTable total also passed. This is an upstream alpha application,
not a guarantee of Excel fidelity or large-workbook performance. Macros,
complex external workbooks and physical printing were not verified.

The Linux i386 build uses Glow and a private libxcb. Native Save As adds
the suggested extension to bare filenames and asks before overwriting an
existing normalized target. Explicit typed extensions are retained.
The original ArtCraft trademarks are not used. Original attribution remains.
No control server or MCP server is started by the package.

Updates use the existing signed APT source and Check & Install Updates.
Removal: sudo apt-get remove gridcraft-vaio (documents/settings are retained).
